  {
    "id": "samf-junior-2002-r2-09",
    "bank": "samf",
    "source": {
      "contest": "South African Mathematics Olympiad",
      "paper": "2002 Junior Round 2",
      "year": 2002,
      "number": 9,
      "url": "https://www.samf.ac.za/content/files/QuestionPapers/j2q2002.pdf"
    },
    "grade": "8-9",
    "points": 5,
    "timeMinutes": null,
    "type": "mc",
    "prompt": "There are ten learners in an environmental club. They have decided to go on shell collection trips. The vehicle with which they undertake the trips can only take eight learners at a time. Each learner goes at least once. What is the minimum number of trips the vehicle must make so that each learner goes on the same number of trips?",
    "image": null,
    "choices": [
      {
        "key": "A",
        "text": "$2$"
      },
      {
        "key": "B",
        "text": "$3$"
      },
      {
        "key": "C",
        "text": "$4$"
      },
      {
        "key": "D",
        "text": "$5$"
      },
      {
        "key": "E",
        "text": "$6$"
      }
    ],
    "answer": "D",
    "acceptedAnswers": null,
    "answerUnit": null,
    "solutions": [
      {
        "title": "Count seats",
        "body": "If there are $m$ trips and each learner goes $t$ times, the number of seats used is $8m$ (a full vehicle each time, since each trip takes $8$) $=10t$. Hence $4m=5t$, so $m$ is a multiple of $5$. The smallest is $m=5$ (with $t=4$).\n\nThis is possible: in each trip leave out a different pair of learners, e.g. trip $i$ leaves out learners $2i-1$ and $2i$. Each learner is then left out once and goes on $4$ trips.\n\n**Answer: (D) 5**"
      }
    ],
    "topics": [
      "number-theory",
      "counting"
    ],
    "difficulty": 2,
    "duplicateOf": null,
    "reviewNote": null,
    "wrongPoints": -1
  },
  {
