        "title": "Choose two lines from $A$ and a horizontal level",
        "body": "Every triangle has vertex $A$, with two of the $7$ lines through $A$ as its sides, cut off by one of the $3$ horizontal lines (the two drawn lines and the base $BC$).\n\nNumber of pairs of lines from $A$: $\\binom72=21$. Number of horizontal cuts: $3$.\n\nTotal $21\\times3=63$.\n\n**Answer: (C) 63**"
