    "points": 5,
    "timeMinutes": null,
    "type": "mc",
    "prompt": "A company makes solid blocks with square bases. The volume of this block is $640\\ \\text{cm}^3$. Its height is $10$ cm. The cost of painting all the faces of this block at $15$c per $\\text{cm}^2$ is",
    "image": "qimages/samf/junior-2002-r2/q14.webp",
    "choices": [
      {
        "key": "A",
        "text": "R64.00"
      },
      {
        "key": "B",
        "text": "R67.20"
      },
      {
        "key": "C",
        "text": "R70.40"
      },
      {
        "key": "D",
        "text": "R73.60"
      },
      {
        "key": "E",
        "text": "R60.20"
      }
    ],
    "answer": "B",
    "acceptedAnswers": null,
    "answerUnit": null,
    "solutions": [
      {
        "title": "Surface area",
        "body": "Base area $=640\\div10=64\\ \\text{cm}^2$, so the base side is $8$ cm. Surface area $=2\\times64+4\\times(8\\times10)=128+320=448\\ \\text{cm}^2$.\n\nCost $=448\\times15\\text{c}=6720\\text{c}=$ R67.20.\n\n**Answer: (B) R67.20**"
      }
    ],
