    "type": "mc",
    "prompt": "The mean (average) of $n$ numbers is $p$. When the number $q$ is removed from the list of numbers averaged, then the mean (average) increases by $2$. The value of $q$ is",
    "image": null,
    "choices": [
      {
        "key": "A",
        "text": "$p-2n$"
      },
      {
        "key": "B",
        "text": "$p-n+2$"
      },
      {
        "key": "C",
        "text": "$2p-n$"
      },
      {
        "key": "D",
        "text": "$2p-n+2$"
      },
      {
        "key": "E",
        "text": "$p-2n+2$"
      }
    ],
    "answer": "E",
    "acceptedAnswers": null,
    "answerUnit": null,
    "solutions": [
      {
        "title": "Sums",
        "body": "The sum of the $n$ numbers is $np$. After removing $q$ there are $n-1$ numbers with mean $p+2$:\n\n$np-q=(n-1)(p+2)=np+2n-p-2$, so $q=p-2n+2$.\n\n**Answer: (E) $p-2n+2$**"
      }
    ],
