        "text": "$5x+1$"
      },
      {
        "key": "E",
        "text": "$2x+1$"
      }
    ],
    "answer": "C",
    "acceptedAnswers": null,
    "answerUnit": null,
    "solutions": [
      {
        "title": "Find the linear key",
        "body": "Values: S$=4$, R$=1$, X$=3$, B$=2$ and G$=14$, O$=5$, L$=11$, D$=8$.\n\nWe need a key $ax+b$ with $f(4)=14$, $f(1)=5$, $f(3)=11$, $f(2)=8$. Going from $x=1$ to $x=2$ the value goes $5\\to8$, a step of $3$, so $a=3$ and $b=5-3=2$: $f(x)=3x+2$. Check: $f(3)=11$, $f(4)=14$.\n\n**Answer: (C) $3x+2$**"
      }
